codemap 9
tour feature-filter-symbols
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note In the Symbols tab, type in the filter field to narrow the list to symbols whose name contains the text, or every symbol of a file whose path contains it, ignoring case; every keystroke re-filters and scrolls the list back to its top. The reader reaches for it to find a symbol or file by name in a large repo without scrolling every file. The toolbar shows 'n of m' while filtering. Symbols sit under a row per file with its covered/total count; each symbol row shows a check when a tour covers the symbol, its name, line and kind. Clicking a symbol row focuses that symbol: when it is a whole-symbol step of the tour being read, that step is selected; otherwise the Source view opens on it, or, on the Tour or Graph tab, the document stays and the status bar says the symbol is off the tour. Clicking a file row opens that file in the Source view.

